users/gordthompson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gordthompson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gordthompson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-03-01T17:20:25Z","updated_at":"2021-03-01T17:20:25Z","body":"Thanks. With your updated code the issue can be reproduced in both 1.3.23 and 1.4 (current master branch). The SQL being emitted is correct. In 1.4 it is\r\n\r\n```sql\r\nSELECT \"TestTable1\".status AS \"TestTable1_status\", array_agg(\"TestTable1\".action ORDER BY \"TestTable1\".priority ASC) AS array_agg_1 \r\nFROM \"TestTable1\" GROUP BY \"TestTable1\".status\r\n```\r\n\r\nand returns reasonable-looking results when executed from DBeaver\r\n\r\n```text\r\nTestTable1_status|array_agg_1    |\r\n-----------------|---------------|\r\nPR Open          |{Accept,Reject}|\r\n```\r\n\r\nso it is a question of how those results are being re-packaged by ORM.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/788123008/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"gordthompson","id":15894006,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1ODk0MDA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15894006?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gordthompson","html_url":"https://github.com/gordthompson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gordthompson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gordthompson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gordthompson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gordthompson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gordthompson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gordthompson/orgs","repos_url":"htt